    "body": "## Carlisle Job Discovery\n\nBuilds the first scalable public discovery flow on top of the Carlisle technical baseline.\n\n### Backend\n- replaces the unbounded public jobs list with a stable paginated response envelope\n- adds text search across title, description and public location label\n- adds minimum/maximum price filters\n- validates pagination bounds, query length and price ranges\n- keeps deterministic newest-first ordering\n- preserves location privacy: public discovery never exposes exact coordinates or private location labels\n\n### PostgreSQL\n- adds Flyway V4\n- enables `pg_trgm`\n- adds partial GIN trigram indexes for open-job title, description and public location label\n- adds an open-job price/created-at index\n\n### Web\n- replaces the placeholder jobs page with real API-backed discovery\n- adds search and price filters\n- adds loading, error and empty states\n- adds reusable job cards and pagination controls\n- adds responsive customer-facing styling while keeping Carlisle as an internal technical milestone name\n\n### Documentation\n- documents the public pagination/filter contract\n- documents indexing and privacy behavior\n- links discovery architecture from the main README\n\n### Verification\n- unit tests for pagination metadata and invalid price ranges\n- Maven verify\n- npm production audit, lint and build\n- Docker runtime smoke verifies PostGIS + pg_trgm, escrow, paginated discovery, filters, privacy, nearby matching and Nginx gateway\n\nThe PR is used as a CI gate. Final `master` history will be fast-forwarded to a single Carlisle commit authored/committed by `jedreekPrograms`, without a GitHub `web-flow` merge commit.",
